      "decisionSummary": "Taxon scotica (monotypic, with hibernica as a synonym) is treated as a species separate from Lagopus lagopus based on differences in plumage, moult patterns, and genome-wide DNA data (Quintela et al. 2010; Kozma et al. 2019; Sangster et al. 2022b). The genetic study of Kozma et al. (2019) suggests that plumage similarities between taxon L. scotica and L. l. variegata are likely convergent, and that the placement of scotica within L. lagopus sensu lato based on mitochondrial DNA data (Gutiérrez et al. 2002) is likely due to mitochondrial DNA artifacts. A detailed comparison of vocalizations to support this split is lacking and clarification on the status of hibernica is needed.",
