      "birdsOfTheWorldUrl": "",
      "decisionSummary": "Taxon mauretanicus is treated as a subspecies of Puffinus yelkouan based on analysis of genomic data (Ferrer Obiol et al. 2021, 2023), supported by mitochondrial DNA (Genovart et al. 2005, 2012), and phenotypic data (Genovart et al. 2012). Both mitochondrial DNA and genomic data indicate relatively low levels of differentiation, comparable to, or lower than, reported for P. puffinus subspecies (Genovart et al. 2005; Rodríguez et al. 2020; Ferrer Obiol et al. 2023), and provide evidence of gene flow between mauretanicus and yelkouan; phenotypic traits also show evidence of intermediacy and admixture in mauretanicus (Genovart et al. 2012). Although assortative mating and distinct vocalizations have been reported (Curé et al. 2010), the available evidence is insufficient to confirm species-level differences.",
