      "decisionSummary": "Taxon obamai is treated as a monotypic species separate from Nystalus striolatus (polytypic, including torridus) following Whitney et al. (2013). While the vocalizations of obamai are distinctive, diagnostic plumage and morphological characters are mostly lacking, and genetic data have produced conflicting results. Contra the preliminary mitochondrial DNA data of Whitney et al. (2013), broader geographic sampling (Duarte 2015) did not recover obamai or striolatus as monophyletic clades, and genomic data (Ferreira 2018) are limited. Furthermore, issues of data quality, small sample sizes, and mislabeling (e.g., Annex 1, Duarte 2015), indicate the need for a thorough genetic review of this complex.",
