      "decisionSummary": "Three species are recognized in the Collared/Fiery-billed Aracari complex (Pteroglossus torquatus/P. frantzii) based mostly on patterns of genetic divergence (Eberhard & Bermingham 2005; Patel et al. 2011) and extent of hybridization at contact zones (Haffer 1967, 1974; Ridgely & Greenfield 2001): polytypic Pteroglossus torquatus (including erythrozonus and nuchalis), which is the most distinctive taxon based on mitochondrial-dominated DNA data and forms a narrow hybrid zone with P. erythropygius sanguineus; monotypic P. frantzii that is parapatric, or narrowly sympatric, with P. torquatus without evidence of hybridization; and polytypic P. erythropygius, including sanguineus, as these taxa appear to form a narrow hybrid zone and exhibit minimal mtDNA divergence from each other. Further research based on nuclear or genomic data would be informative.",
