      "decisionSummary": "Corvus torquatus Lesson, 1831 is the correct name for the Collared Crow. The usage of Corvus pectoralis for this species is based on the interpretation that Corvus torquatus Lesson, 1831 is a junior synonym of \"Corvus Monedula torquata\" Bechstein, 1791. However, Bechstein (1791) used the word \"torquata\" for an aberration, not for a taxonomic unit, as explicitly mentioned in his text and as shown in his capitalization practice for taxonomic units only. His introduction of \"torquata\" is not a legitimate nomenclatural taxon description, rendering Corvus torquatus Lesson, 1831 the senior name for the Collared Crow.",
