      "decisionSummary": "Taxa within the Zosterops maderaspatanus complex are treated as conspecific based on available evidence. Sometimes split into four species (polytypic maderaspatanus, and monotypic comorensis, anjuanensis, and aldabrensis) on the basis of morphological and vocal differences, based on mitochondrial DNA data (Warren et al. 2006; Melo et al. 2011; Martins et al. 2020) they form a poorly resolved cluster along with Z. mayottensis and Z. kirki. In the absence of clear phenotypic, behavioral, or ecological criteria to delimit species within the Z. maderaspatanus complex, the four taxa are best retained as a single species pending further research. A thorough vocal analysis and a genomic DNA perspective would be informative.",
