      "decisionSummary": "2025-0171)) Taxon stejnegeri is treated as conspecific with Saxicola maurus pending further research. Although mitochondrial DNA data (Zink et al. 2009; Illera et al. 2008) indicate the presence of deep divergences within the Asian stonechats, not all taxa have been sampled. Furthermore, unsampled taxa have senior scientific names and may be closely related to stejnegeri; consequently, the split of stejnegeri is considered premature; genomic data required. 2025-0172)) Saxicola torquatus is treated as three species based on available evidence: S. maurus (Asian stonechats, polytypic); S. torquatus (African stonechats, polytypic); and S. rubicola (European stonechats, polytypic). Genomic (Van Doren et al. 2017) and mitochondrial DNA data (Zink et al. 2009; Illera et al. 2008) do not recover S. torquatus sensu lato as monophyletic, with S. dacotiae embedded within it. A more comprehensive taxonomic review of this complex is required given the ecological and phenotypic similarities among these species.",
